 "note": "Round 13 (re-proportioned): the full hair mop (hair_cut 35, fringe_x .1: face in front, hair behind), a SMALL beanie on top of the hair (cap_f .8, cap_dy 1.1; it used to be a dome over half the head) and a smaller head (head_r 4.6). The Beenie (beenie.py): the kid rig in blue with a three-gore propeller beanie and a green blaster; faces right f66-f77, turns f78-f79, left f80-f108, front/back f109-f121 (from the blaster position). Round 10 first verify: 0/56, IoU 0.708, dE 31. Per-row widths (f80): source head+beanie 12 px wide over rows 5-11, body 9-11, legs 7-9, feet 6-8; ours: head 7-9, the blaster rows 17 (vs 11), feet 14. fm_diag f70: the source cap shows all three gores (R left, B middle, G right) where ours shows only red; the source shoes are red with skin shins above. Needs re-proportioning from a per-row survey (bigger head, slimmer body and blaster, small red shoes, cap_turn) before any fit. Round 13 (viewed zoomed heads): the Beenie is a WHITE-FACED CLOWN -- white face, dark blue eye sockets, a big red smile, a small cap dome on top with the red propeller; ours had a peach face and a cap dome over half the head -> skin white, dark eyes, mouth_r 3, cap raised (cap_dy .5) and smaller.",
